\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Sampling and the balance of vertex degrees}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{For nondegenerate zero vertices, \ref{fdip-0140} balances their degrees
against an aggregate off-grid degree. When do all zeros lie at vertices, and which
integer replaces the balance for a Hermitian symbol of any size on a grid of dimension #{n\ge 2}?}

\p{The statements on Clifford symbols hold over an ordered field, or over the real numbers
where trigonometric polynomials occur, in any dimension #{n}. The statements on Hermitian
symbols hold over the complex numbers, in any dimension #{n\ge 2}, for any finite dimension of
the complex space and any number #{q\ge 1} of negative eigenvalues. The cancellation around
singular vertices needs #{n\ge 3}.}
